# pgmpy Cline Rules

Rules for AI agents using Cline/Windsurf/Antigravity interfaces.

## ⚡ Pre-Flight Checklist
Before any task:
- [ ] Read `.cursorrules` for code patterns
- [ ] Check `ARCHITECTURE.md` for project structure
- [ ] Identify target files and test locations
- [ ] Plan changes before editing

## 🎯 Task Priority Matrix

| Priority | Task Type | Action |
|----------|-----------|--------|
| 🔴 High | Bug fix | Reproduce → Fix → Test → PR |
| 🟡 Medium | Feature | Plan → Implement → Test → PR |
| 🟢 Low | Docs | Update → Verify links → PR |

## ✅ Safe Commands (Auto-run OK)
```bash
pytest                    # Run tests
pytest pgmpy/tests/ -v   # Verbose tests
ruff check .             # Lint
ruff format .            # Format
git status               # Check status
git diff                 # View changes
pip list                 # Check packages
```

## ⚠️ Requires Approval
```bash
git push                 # Pushing changes
pip install <pkg>        # New dependencies
rm -rf <dir>             # Deletions
```

## 📁 Quick File Finder

| Need to... | Go to... |
|------------|----------|
| Add model | `pgmpy/models/` |
| Add factor/CPD | `pgmpy/factors/` |
| Add estimator | `pgmpy/estimators/` |
| Add inference | `pgmpy/inference/` |
| Add I/O format | `pgmpy/readwrite/` |
| Add tests | `pgmpy/tests/test_<module>/` |

## 🔧 Component Quick Reference

### Models
`DiscreteBayesianNetwork` `LinearGaussianBayesianNetwork` `FunctionalBayesianNetwork` `NaiveBayes` `DynamicBayesianNetwork` `DiscreteMarkovNetwork` `FactorGraph` `ClusterGraph` `SEM` `MarkovChain` `JunctionTree`

### Factors
`TabularCPD` `DiscreteFactor` `JointProbabilityDistribution` `NoisyOR` `LinearGaussianCPD` `FunctionalCPD`

### Estimators
`MLE` `BayesianEstimator` `EM` `PC` `HillClimbSearch` `GES` `ExhaustiveSearch` `TreeSearch` `MmhcEstimator`

### Inference
`VariableElimination` `BeliefPropagation` `DBNInference` `ApproxInference` `CausalInference` `Mplp`

## 🚫 Anti-Patterns

| DON'T | DO |
|-------|-----|
| Use `unittest` | Use `pytest` |
| Loop over rows | Vectorize with NumPy/Pandas |
| Skip docstrings | Use numpydoc format |
| Add core deps | Use optional extras |
| Delete tests | Add more tests |
| Modify public API | Discuss first |

## 🔄 Standard Workflow
```
1. git checkout -b feature/name dev
2. Write failing test
3. Implement feature
4. ruff check . && pytest
5. git commit -m "feat: description"
6. Create PR against dev
```

## 📊 CI/CD Info
- **Tests**: Python 3.10-3.14 on Ubuntu/Windows/macOS
- **Lint**: Ruff via `lint.yml`
- **Security**: CodeQL via `codeql.yml`
